 "body": "Given the following code:\n\n```\nvoid setup() {\n  int v = 4385;\n  String s(v, HEX);\n} \n\nvoid loop() { }\n```\n\nthe current overloading of the String constructor causes the error:\n\nsketch_apr01a:3: error: call of overloaded \u2018String(int&, int)\u2019 is ambiguous\n/home/matt/git/Arduino/build/linux/work/hardware/arduino/cores/arduino/WString.h:72: note: candidates are: String::String(double, int)\n/home/matt/git/Arduino/build/linux/work/hardware/arduino/cores/arduino/WString.h:71: note:                 String::String(float, int)\n/home/matt/git/Arduino/build/linux/work/hardware/arduino/cores/arduino/WString.h:70: note:                 String::String(long unsigned int, unsigned char)\n/home/matt/git/Arduino/build/linux/work/hardware/arduino/cores/arduino/WString.h:69: note:                 String::String(long int, unsigned char)\n/home/matt/git/Arduino/build/linux/work/hardware/arduino/cores/arduino/WString.h:68: note:                 String::String(unsigned int, unsigned char)\n/home/matt/git/Arduino/build/linux/work/hardware/arduino/cores/arduino/WString.h:67: note:                 String::String(int, unsigned char)\n/home/matt/git/Arduino/build/linux/work/hardware/arduino/cores/arduino/WString.h:66: note:                 String::String(unsigned char, unsigned char)\n\nSwitching the float/double decimal places parameter to an unsigned char like the rest of the constructors resolves the issue.\n",
